WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:08.320
This is how you should be warping to the&nbsp;
Roundtable Hold. Done. It's that easy! Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.880
be honest, how many of you are still&nbsp;
dragging your cursor there manually? Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.160
you should press triangle or Y to open the list&nbsp;
of grace checkpoints, then you press square or x&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.520
to confirm a warp straight there. It took me..way&nbsp;
too long to discover that this was a thing. 
&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.560
Elden Ring is full of little quality of life&nbsp;
things like this that are never explained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.120
so I'm going to start this video by&nbsp;
quickfiring five more at you. 
&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.040
For example, if you walk through a beacon of&nbsp;
light that you've placed..then that beacon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.080
will disappear. This is an excellent way to mark&nbsp;
that actually you've reached your destination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.480
without having to pull up your map. 
Next, if an enemy explodes in a burst of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.760
blue light, that means they're going&nbsp;
to drop an item. Don't miss it.
&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:54.800
When you pick up an item, take note of this icon.&nbsp;
This tells you which category of your inventory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.840
that item just went into. This will make it way&nbsp;
easier to figure out what you just picked up.
&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.240
Another great way to find what you just picked up&nbsp;
is to press L3 on the inventory menu. This will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.840
let you sort in order of acquisition, and look&nbsp;
over all the items that you recently looted.
&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.760
By default though, your inventory is sorted into&nbsp;
vertical categories, demarcated by horizontal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.880
lines. For example, the bolstering materials&nbsp;
tab organises your crimson flask materials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.880
your smithing stones and your somber smithing&nbsp;
stones into their own sections. 
&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.480
Now with those quality of life tips out of&nbsp;
the way...let's get into the big stuff. 
&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.600
First, how would you like to have a&nbsp;
buff that gives you 5% extra runes?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.880
To get this, all you have to&nbsp;
do is type in 7 letters.
&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:50.960
In the last video, I announced "Secret Seekers",&nbsp;
our community group password. Enter "SEEKERS" in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.840
all caps as your first group password in your&nbsp;
multiplayer tab, and you'll be able to identify&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.240
phantoms, bloodstains, messages and summon signs&nbsp;
from others in the group. Our goal is to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:08.000
secrets in the game, and share them with others.&nbsp;
Since then, I can't go 5 minutes without finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:16.880
evidence of you guys hurling yourself off cliffs&nbsp;
in search of secrets. You make me so proud.
&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.760
Since then, we also discovered that every time&nbsp;
someone in the group defeats a shardbearer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:27.120
or becomes Elden Lord, everyone else in the group&nbsp;
receives a 5% buff to their rune acquisition..and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:34.000
considering there are thousands of you in this&nbsp;
group..this buff activates like..constantly. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.760
join us, and enjoy your free runes.
Also..I put the SECRET SEEKERS logo onto a shirt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.560
So, if you want to rep our unofficial covenant&nbsp;
- check it out with the link below. 
&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.920
Another way to get free runes is by duplicating&nbsp;
your remembrances. Goddrick's, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.200
gives 20,000 - and subsequent bosses give&nbsp;
even more than that. Every major boss drops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.840
a remembrance, though the proper way to use&nbsp;
these is to trade them in for boss items at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.440
Enia, the Finger Reader at Roundtable Hold. 
Because each remembrance can be traded for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:11.280
multiple items, it's possible to duplicate them at&nbsp;
the walking mausoleums found throughout the game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:17.120
Here's what some of our testing revealed:
First, there are six mausoleums in total. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.960
in Limgrave ... Three in Liurnia ... one&nbsp;
in Mountaintops of the Giants ... and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:30.800
in the Consecrated Snowfield. The method of&nbsp;
bringing down a mausoleum differs in some cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.160
but it's generally related to removing&nbsp;
the white curse marks from its body.
&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.640
It's worth finding your way up to each&nbsp;
of these, because you can only duplicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.840
one remembrance per mausoleum. After duplicating,&nbsp;
that mausoleum becomes pretty obsolete.
&nbsp;

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.000
interestingly, you don't actually&nbsp;
need the remembrance in your inventory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.400
to duplicate it - you just have to have&nbsp;
defeated the boss you got it from. 
&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.640
Also, note that you cannot duplicate&nbsp;
remembrances that you have already claimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:02.000
all the items from.
And make sure you use your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:07.280
duplications before heading to NG+, because your&nbsp;
remaining duplications won't carry over.
&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.760
In addition to getting a remembrance, defeating&nbsp;
a shardbearer will also grant you a Great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:19.280
Rune. Once acquired, you have to go to its&nbsp;
corresponding Divine Tower and "activate" it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.800
After doing this you can "equip" a great rune at a&nbsp;
site of lost grace, with your equipped great rune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.280
appearing in the top left of your screen.
These Great Runes bestow powerful effects upon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.960
your character - though equipping the rune doesn't&nbsp;
actually apply its effects - instead, to do that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:40.800
you'll need to consume a "Rune Arc". These&nbsp;
powerful consumables are a reward for invading,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:53.680
doing co-op, exploring the world..and killing&nbsp;
rats. Yeah. Rats. Just like they drop humanity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.160
in the Souls games, they also drop Rune Arcs&nbsp;
sometimes. The lore here is that even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:03.760
most valuable items make their way down to&nbsp;
the bottom rung of the food chain..to these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.800
creatures that consume the bodies of all. 
Every great rune does something different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.400
Godrick's, for example, increases&nbsp;
every one of your attributes by 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:21.600
essentially granting you 40 extra levels.&nbsp;
Characters that use a wide variety of spells and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.120
scalings will benefit most from this, and some of&nbsp;
the later great runes are even more powerful. 
&nbsp;

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:34.480
Without a Great Rune equipped, a rune arc&nbsp;
will increase your max HP by about 10%. All of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.080
these effects persist through warping, which is&nbsp;
great - and will last until death, or re-equipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.943
a Great Rune. Essentially it's Elden&nbsp;
Ring's equivalent of being embered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.943 --> 00:05:41.360
or having your hollowing reversed.
So remember: make use of Rune Arcs. Don't just let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:50.000
them sit wasted in your inventory. Equip them to&nbsp;
your pouch, and pop one whenever you're on a very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.960
difficult boss. It might turn out that a Rune Arc&nbsp;
could tip you just over the edge, to victory. 
&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.120
Rennala's Great Rune is a bit of an outlier.&nbsp;
Unlike the others, it can't be equipped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:07.040
and it doesn't need to be activated by a Rune Arc.&nbsp;
Rather, it can be used to respec your character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:10.800
Talk to Rennala at Raya Lucaria, and&nbsp;
you'll be able to bring your character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.680
back to their starting stats, with all your&nbsp;
previous levels ready for reinvestment. 
&nbsp;

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.000
This process requires that you defeat&nbsp;
Rennala of course, but also that you have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.840
Larval Tear. These are very rare, but to tell you&nbsp;
about the location of at least one - there's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.760
royal soldier located here in Limgrave..that&nbsp;
drops one. Be careful though..kill him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.560
and he might just be reborn anew. 
Elden Ring is a long game. So..consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:43.440
switching things up! I mean..they keep giving&nbsp;
me spells that my melee character can't use! So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.040
you know what..maybe shooting&nbsp;
meteorites does sound like fun.
&nbsp;

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.520
Another way to fix your character might be&nbsp;
via pardoning, which - let's be honest - is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.080
a mechanic that exists for when you put down your&nbsp;
controller and accidentally press the R2 button&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:06.560
in front of an NPC. Alternatively, it's also&nbsp;
useful when giant dogs attack NPCs through walls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:11.520
and they get upset at you, instead. 
That said..most important NPCs can't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:19.520
attacked in this game...so what is&nbsp;
this for, really? In testing this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:24.640
I realised..it must be for the merchants.
&nbsp;

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.080
Because logically - you should be killing&nbsp;
every merchant you see. Once you kill them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:36.080
you can just buy all of their items in one place,&nbsp;
at the Twin Maiden husks at Roundtable hold. 
&nbsp;

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:46.160
That said..it's very traumatising to&nbsp;
kill a merchant. Just listen to him. 
&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.640
So, if you regret this&nbsp;
decision - ask for forgiveness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.920
and the merchant will become friendly again. 
If you really do have some angst to let out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:02.320
don't take it out on NPCs that don't&nbsp;
really exist - take it out on other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:07.200
human beings, instead, like a normal person.
Your item for infinite invasions is the Bloody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:12.320
Finger, which can be acquired by progressing&nbsp;
Varre's questline to the Rose Church. 
&nbsp;

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.160
Speak to him before defeating Goddrick, then&nbsp;
again afterwards at Roundtable Hold, then at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:21.760
the Rose Church in Liurnia, located here.&nbsp;
Here he'll give you five festering bloody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.080
fingers for invading other players - use&nbsp;
three of them to progress his questline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:31.280
where he will next require you to soak the Lord&nbsp;
of Blood's favour in the blood of a maiden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:36.720
One exists in the Church of Inhbition located&nbsp;
here, in Liurnia. Interact with the maiden, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.000
return to Varre to receive the Bloody Finger. 
Alternatively, you can pick up the Recusant's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:47.760
Finger at the Volcano Manor - and this&nbsp;
one has a different story affiliation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:53.520
to the invaders of the Bloody Finger. 
But if you'd rather engage in duels with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:58.400
other players, then you'll need the Duelist's&nbsp;
Furled Finger, which can be found on a corpse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:03.200
at the doors of the Stormhill Colosseum.&nbsp;
The Small Red Effigy can also be found here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.880
which serves the same purpose, except it sends&nbsp;
a competitive summon sign to the Summoning Pool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.160
instead. Summoning pools are accessible at&nbsp;
these effigies, found throughout the world. 
&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.960
And if PvP is something you'd like to&nbsp;
avoid - well, pick up the white cipher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:23.040
ring from the Twin Maiden Husks at the&nbsp;
Roundtable hold. With this buff active,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.680
you'll automatically request help from another&nbsp;
player when your world is invaded. If you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:33.120
to BE the player that helps invaded players, then&nbsp;
you can use the Blue Cipher Ring, instead. 
&nbsp;

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.280
Also in the Roundtable Hold is Fia,&nbsp;
the Deathbed Companion. Embrace her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.000
and you'll receive a Baldachin's Blessing. 
Now...and it's startling that not many people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.240
realise this - but did you know that&nbsp;
your health is reduced while you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:52.560
have the blessing in your inventory?
That's right, you lose a few points of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:57.440
your vigor stat - essentially around 5% health, a&nbsp;
debuff that remains UNTIL you use her Baldachin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.110
Blessing. There's gotta be some people in the&nbsp;
comments that have kept this thing in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:01.040
inventory for hours without a second thought,&nbsp;
I guarantee it. And I don't blame you! The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:07.120
buff/debuff icons are pretty intense in this&nbsp;
game - as a side note - icons with a square&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.480
around them are permanent effects from rings, and&nbsp;
ones with diamonds around them are temporary. 
&nbsp;

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:16.800
But the biggest question is - is the&nbsp;
Baldachin's Blessing worth it? And..the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:22.560
is..kind of? Sometimes? The Baldachin's&nbsp;
Blessing essentially gives you a type of poise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:29.360
for about 15 seconds. This is extremely useful&nbsp;
when you're facing a lot of minor enemies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:34.960
as you'll completely ignore their small attacks&nbsp;
and only get staggered by their strong attacks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:40.400
However, the blessing seems pretty pointless&nbsp;
when facing a single enemy, or any large enemy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:45.600
So I'd honestly only really recommend bothering&nbsp;
with this item if you KNOW that extra poise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:50.160
will serve you well in an encounter to&nbsp;
come - like in a cave with lots of rats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.280
or demi-humans, or flying projectiles. 
But the main reason to go back to Fia every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.280 --> 00:11:00.080
now and again..is because you'll eventually get&nbsp;
a dialogue option for progressing her questline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.920
For me, this always appears once I've&nbsp;
moved into the Altus Plateau. 
&nbsp;

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:10.080
Also, enjoy the cuddles. Or don't. You can&nbsp;
also just warp out of them if you think the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.840
animation is too long. Though things like&nbsp;
this are why you're maidenless, you know.
&nbsp;

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.720
For number 14, have you ever found yourself&nbsp;
disappointed with the amount of armours that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.520
you can alter? Well, you can actually expand&nbsp;
your options by acquiring the Gold Sewing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:28.640
Needle in Liurnia, in a chest to the right when&nbsp;
you enter the Church of Vows, located here. 
&nbsp;

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:40.080
Furthermore, if you progressed Boc's questline&nbsp;
in Limgrave after talking to him here...and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:46.720
here...then you'll find him again in&nbsp;
Liurnia, at the East Raya Lucaria Gate. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:51.200
Boc will perform your armour alterations for&nbsp;
you for free, even taking the Gold Sewing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.200 --> 00:12:00.640
Needle from you, if you should so desire. 
Finally..everyone knows about the whetstone knife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.440
at the Gateside Ruins that lets you apply&nbsp;
ashes of war - but did you know that there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.594 --> 00:12:23.514
or quality scaling...and is located in Stormveil&nbsp;
castle - or the glintstone whetblade, which adds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.514 --> 00:12:29.114
magic scaling, located in Raya Lucaria. 
Thank you for watching. Special thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.114 --> 00:12:32.074
to Absa who helped me with some&nbsp;
of the research for this video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.634 --> 00:12:39.594
Again, check out our Secret Seekers covenant and&nbsp;
merch if you're interested - and i'll see you next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.594 --> 00:12:42.074
time. 

